---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { SERVICE_BRANCHES } from "../../config/services";
import { SITE_NAME } from "../../config/site";
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`Services — ${SITE_NAME}`}
  description="Training in self-directed learning, and agentic harness automation for a team or a single engineer."
  section="services"
>
  <p class="section-label">Services</p>
  <h1 class="page-title">Two kinds of leverage, offered as work.</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    The blog covers how this is built. These are the same two threads as engagements: the method
    for teaching yourself a skill, and the harness that makes a coding agent worth handing work to.
  </p>

  <ul class="service-grid">
    {SERVICE_BRANCHES.map((branch) => (
      <li class="service-card">
        <p class="service-card__kicker">{branch.label}</p>
        <h2>{branch.tagline}</h2>
        <p>{branch.description}</p>
        <ul class="service-card__list">
          {branch.offerings.map((offering) => (
            <li>{offering.title}</li>
          ))}
        </ul>
        <a class="read-more" href={`/services/${branch.slug}/`}>
          {branch.label} details &rarr;
        </a>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ul>

  <section class="cta-panel">
    <h2>Enquiring about an engagement</h2>
    <p>
      This runs alongside a full-time job, so I keep a hard cap of two concurrent engagements and
      review new enquiries in batches rather than as they arrive. The waitlist is how that queue
      works.
    </p>
    <a class="cta-panel__action" href="/waitlist/">Join the waitlist &rarr;</a>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
